1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,875
If the Moon
vanished tonight,

2
00:00:01,895 --> 00:00:04,179
would Earth go flying
off into space?

3
00:00:04,969 --> 00:00:07,297
Earth and the Moon
circle a shared balance

4
00:00:07,317 --> 00:00:07,903
point.

5
00:00:07,993 --> 00:00:10,780
It sits inside Earth,
about four thousand seven

6
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,140
hundred kilometers
from the center.

7
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:16,705
Each month, Earth loops
around it at only about

8
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:18,461
twelve meters
per second.

9
00:00:19,251 --> 00:00:20,837
Our speed
around the Sun?

10
00:00:20,927 --> 00:00:23,233
Nearly thirty
kilometers per second.

11
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:26,099
So without the Moon,
that little loop just

12
00:00:26,119 --> 00:00:27,167
straightens out.

13
00:00:27,257 --> 00:00:29,189
Our orbit
barely changes.

14
00:00:29,979 --> 00:00:32,729
The real changes are
slower, and stranger.

15
00:00:32,819 --> 00:00:34,737
The full story is
on our channel:

16
00:00:34,757 --> 00:00:36,284
The Moon
Vanishes Tonight.
